@engagement = http://localhost:4002

### Redeem coins for a store item (workflow steps 6-7)
# Inside the POST: order recorded (stock and limit decremented, price and reward frozen), then a synchronous
# coin reserve in payments. The casino reward is issued afterwards by the sweeper through the adapter port,
# with our idempotency key redeem:<id>. The POST never calls the casino.
# @name redeem
POST {{engagement}}/v1/redemptions
Authorization: Bearer {{player_token}}
Idempotency-Key: redeem-0001-player-77
Content-Type: application/json

{ "item_id": "0190...-item" }

# Response: expected, to be replaced with captured output
# HTTP/1.1 201 Created   (202 Accepted if the reserve call timed out; the sweeper repeats it with the same key)
# {
#   "id": "0190...-redemption", "item_id": "0190...-item", "price": 40,
#   "status": "pending", "state": "RESERVED", "attempts": 0,
#   "casino_reference": null, "failure_reason": null,
#   "history": [ { "from": null, "to": "REQUESTED", "cause": "order", "at": "2026-11-21T10:10:00.000Z" },
#                { "from": "REQUESTED", "to": "RESERVED", "cause": "reserve ok", "at": "2026-11-21T10:10:00.100Z" } ],
#   "created_at": "2026-11-21T10:10:00.000Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-21T10:10:00.100Z"
# }

### Not enough coins: the player sees it at once (decision D-8)
POST {{engagement}}/v1/redemptions
Authorization: Bearer {{poor_player_token}}
Idempotency-Key: redeem-0002-player-12
Content-Type: application/json

{ "item_id": "0190...-item" }

# Response: expected, to be replaced with captured output
# HTTP/1.1 409 Conflict
# { "code": "insufficient_funds", "message": "..." }
# Stock and per-player limit are put back; no casino call was made.

### Out of stock
# HTTP/1.1 409 Conflict  { "code": "out_of_stock", "message": "..." }
